<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h1 class="display-4 fw-bold mb-3">Hostel & Boarding Management</h1>
        <p class="lead mb-4">
            A high-standard pastoral engine that secures and organizes life in the boarding 
            house—managing dormitory logistics and student welfare with professional precision.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Dormitory & Facility Oversight</h2>
        <p>
            Experience perfect organizational visibility into your boarding infrastructure. The 
            Boarding module allows for the granular management of dormitories, houses, 
            and specific bed assignments. Hostel staff can monitor room occupancy across 
            the campus, facilitating rapid student check-in during term starts and 
            maintaining a complete historical record of boarding placements.
        </p>
        <p>
            Boarding-specific fee schedules are hard-wired into the student finance account, 
            ensuring that hostel and meal charges are captured accurately based on 
            assigned accommodation levels.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Pastoral Welfare & exeat Workflow</h2>
        <p>
            Digitize the student leave application process. The exeat workflow allows students 
            or parents to request weekend or mid-term leave through the portal, with a 
            structured approval path through House Masters and the Principal. Once 
            approved, parents receive immediate confirmation via WhatsApp, providing 
            an authoritative digital trail for any student departure from campus.
        </p>
        <p>
            Nightly roll-call logs and shift handover reports provide the boarding 
            stewardship team with a real-time view of student presence and health 
            incidents, ensuring that welfare standards are maintained across the 
            24-hour cycle.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Health & Dietary Communication</h2>
        <p>
            Maintain a safe and responsive boarding environment. The system maintains a 
            high-visibility alert registry for boarders with specific medical conditions 
            or dietary requirements, visible to house mothers and catering staff 
            (where authorized). Direct parent contact triggers for health or welfare 
            incidents ensure that the school remains in constant, professional communication 
            with the family whenever a boarder requires additional attention.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

